WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.829 --> 00:00:07.753
Do you know anyone who is physically handicapped?

2
00:00:08.934 --> 00:00:15.839
It is not easy to overcome a handicap, but many handicapped people do lead successful lives.

3
00:00:16.899 --> 00:00:24.184
Helen Keller was one of them, thanks to the amazing lessons of Anne Sullivan, a partially blind teacher.

4
00:00:25.665 --> 00:00:28.387
Helen Keller was born in America in 1880.

5
00:00:30.012 --> 00:00:35.556
When she was almost two years old, she got sick with an unusually high fever.

6
00:00:36.597 --> 00:00:41.701
Because of the high fever, Helen lost both her sight and her hearing.

7
00:00:42.721 --> 00:00:44.803
Helen's parents were very upset.

8
00:00:44.823 --> 00:00:46.984
"What's wrong with her?

9
00:00:47.425 --> 00:00:49.006
Why can't she see or hear?"

10
00:00:49.546 --> 00:00:51.207
Mrs. Keller asked the doctor.

11
00:00:52.709 --> 00:00:55.330
The doctor explained that nothing could be done.

12
00:00:56.471 --> 00:00:59.845
Soon after, Helen also forgot how to talk.

13
00:01:01.005 --> 00:01:08.668
Before she became sick, Helen was a happy, playful child, but now she acted like a wild animal.

14
00:01:09.829 --> 00:01:12.470
No one could teach her or tell her anything.

15
00:01:14.051 --> 00:01:19.373
When Helen was seven years old, her parents contacted a school for the blind.

16
00:01:20.473 --> 00:01:24.235
The school sent a teacher named Anne Sullivan to visit them.

17
00:01:24.255 --> 00:01:30.918
"Helen has been blind, deaf, and mute for five years," Helen's father told Anne.

18
00:01:30.938 --> 00:01:36.021
"She has had many teachers, but no one has succeeded in helping her."

19
00:01:36.041 --> 00:01:40.723
"I will teach her in a special way," explained Anne.

20
00:01:41.904 --> 00:01:47.447
She knew that Helen was very badly behaved and that teaching her would be difficult.

21
00:01:47.467 --> 00:01:51.189
"Can you promise me that you won't disrupt my teaching?"

22
00:01:51.629 --> 00:01:53.010
she asked Helen's parents.

23
00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:54.331
They agreed.

24
00:01:55.811 --> 00:01:59.534
The next day Anne gave Helen a pretty china doll.

25
00:02:00.715 --> 00:02:06.198
Anne took one of Helen's hands and put it on the doll so that Helen could feel it.

26
00:02:07.339 --> 00:02:14.524
Then Anne used the sign language alphabet to spell the word "doll" on the palm of Helen's hand.

27
00:02:16.325 --> 00:02:18.406
But Helen did not understand.

28
00:02:18.907 --> 00:02:20.428
She thought it was a game.

29
00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:26.272
Helen also acted rudely during meals.

30
00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:29.261
"Helen is throwing things again!"

31
00:02:29.841 --> 00:02:32.783
Mrs. Keller cried when Helen smashed her plate.

32
00:02:33.964 --> 00:02:38.526
Anne watched the scene, surprised but not shocked by Helen's behavior.

33
00:02:38.546 --> 00:02:43.069
"Helen must learn how to sit at the table," she told Mrs.

34
00:02:43.129 --> 00:02:46.190
Keller. "Where can I teach her in private?"

35
00:02:46.210 --> 00:02:49.192
"We have a cabin nearby.

36
00:02:49.592 --> 00:02:52.374
Helen has never been there," said Helen's mother.

37
00:02:53.615 --> 00:02:55.836
Anne took Helen to the nearby cabin.

38
00:02:56.976 --> 00:03:00.438
On the way they walked around the woods for a long time.

39
00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:09.642
Anne wanted Helen to think that the cabin was far, far away from home.

40
00:03:13.023 --> 00:03:17.926
At the cabin Anne worked very hard trying to teach manners to Helen.

41
00:03:19.006 --> 00:03:23.208
When Helen ate wildly one day, Anne took away her food.

42
00:03:24.408 --> 00:03:31.293
Anne finally returned Helen's plate of food, but she did not let Helen eat until she sat still

43
00:03:31.773 --> 00:03:32.794
and used a spoon.

44
00:03:33.975 --> 00:03:37.998
Anne taught Helen table manners every day at every meal.

45
00:03:39.659 --> 00:03:41.200
Several weeks went by.

46
00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:46.063
Finally Helen and Anne were ready to return home for dinner.

47
00:03:47.244 --> 00:03:51.207
When Helen sat still at the table, her mother was amazed.

48
00:03:51.227 --> 00:03:54.453
"Oh! This is a miracle!

49
00:03:55.113 --> 00:03:58.536
I never thought Helen would learn anything again," said Mrs.

50
00:03:58.596 --> 00:04:04.620
Keller. She was even more surprised when Helen also ate her food properly.

51
00:04:06.021 --> 00:04:09.583
Anne kept on trying to teach Helen letters and words.

52
00:04:10.644 --> 00:04:16.728
She picked up the china doll again, spelling "doll" with sign language onto Helen's hand.

53
00:04:17.888 --> 00:04:19.609
Helen was still confused.

54
00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:25.426
She finally got so frustrated and angry, she threw the doll on the floor.

55
00:04:25.446 --> 00:04:28.028
"Oh no!"

56
00:04:28.689 --> 00:04:34.234
said Anne when the doll smashed, but she did not give up trying to teach words to her

57
00:04:34.294 --> 00:04:35.115
young student.

58
00:04:36.637 --> 00:04:39.399
At last something remarkable happened.

59
00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:44.424
Anne used the water pump to show Helen how to spell "water."

60
00:04:45.625 --> 00:04:51.885
Anne put one of Helen's hands under the water and used the sign language alphabet to spell the

61
00:04:51.925 --> 00:04:53.806
word into Helen's other hand.

62
00:04:55.447 --> 00:05:01.989
"W-A-T-E-R," Anne spelled out the word again and again.

63
00:05:06.872 --> 00:05:10.333
Suddenly Helen understood what Anne was doing.

64
00:05:11.513 --> 00:05:15.715
She learned that what came out of the pump was called water.

65
00:05:16.796 --> 00:05:20.665
Right away Helen began touching other things around her.

66
00:05:21.785 --> 00:05:24.526
She wanted to learn the words for everything.

67
00:05:25.626 --> 00:05:32.788
When Helen touched the broken doll, she cried because she understood now what Anne had been trying to

68
00:05:32.848 --> 00:05:33.328
teach her.

69
00:05:34.929 --> 00:05:37.630
Anne was so happy, she hugged Helen.

70
00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:41.211
Her student was finally learning about words!

71
00:05:42.851 --> 00:05:48.765
Anne began to teach Helen how to read and write, and she learned in only three years.

72
00:05:49.965 --> 00:05:52.346
She even began to learn to speak.

73
00:05:54.066 --> 00:06:00.608
Anne and Helen spent many years together, teaching and learning and becoming close friends.

74
00:06:01.788 --> 00:06:06.550
Helen eventually went to several schools and even enrolled in college.

75
00:06:07.770 --> 00:06:14.612
At the age of 24, she became the first deaf and blind person to graduate from college.

76
00:06:15.912 --> 00:06:19.753
Helen spent the rest of her life encouraging and helping people.

77
00:06:20.813 --> 00:06:27.335
Her mission was to help people who, like herself, had lost one or more of their senses.

78
00:06:28.615 --> 00:06:32.997
She also gave hope to soldiers who were handicapped during wartime.

79
00:06:34.137 --> 00:06:37.498
Helen Keller traveled all over the world speaking.

80
00:06:39.178 --> 00:06:45.100
She wrote twelve books, met many famous people, and received important awards.

81
00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:53.905
Because Anne Sullivan had taught and cared for her, Helen grew up to be an amazing woman, even

82
00:06:53.985 --> 00:06:56.466
though she couldn't see or hear.

83
00:06:57.587 --> 00:07:01.149
Think of the teachers who have cared for you and taught you.

84
00:07:02.350 --> 00:07:05.312
Why don't you write one of them a thank-you note today?
